# Context filter for the images built from the REPO ROOT:
# bench/Dockerfile and millrace/Dockerfile, which need the uv workspace
# root (pyproject.toml, uv.lock), pyhoglake/, their own tree and every
# other member's pyproject.toml (they install the client as a workspace
# member from the one lock). server/ and webui/ build from their own
# directories and carry their own .dockerignore files.
#
# The first block is the one that has actually bitten: a host .venv is
# macOS-built binaries, and a copy of it into a linux image either
# fails at import or, worse, shadows the image's own install. Keep it
# out of the context entirely rather than relying on the Dockerfile not
# to COPY it.
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.flox/

.git/
.github/

# Trees neither image installs. Excluded by name so the context stays
# small and a change over there cannot invalidate a layer here; add a
# line if a new top-level tree appears.
server/
webui/
duckdb-client/
docs/
# hedgerow is a workspace member neither image installs, but a --locked
# sync validates the lock against every member's manifest: keep its
# pyproject.toml and nothing else.
hedgerow/*
!hedgerow/pyproject.toml
# Likewise the Rust codec (its cargo target/ is gigabytes): what the
# wheel builds from, which millrace/Dockerfile's codec stage does. Not
# rust-toolchain.toml: the stage's image pins the same Rust.
pyhoglake-variant-codec/*
!pyhoglake-variant-codec/pyproject.toml
!pyhoglake-variant-codec/Cargo.toml
!pyhoglake-variant-codec/Cargo.lock
!pyhoglake-variant-codec/README.md
!pyhoglake-variant-codec/LICENSE
!pyhoglake-variant-codec/src/

# Local run artifacts.
**/bench-results.jsonl
**/*.log
